WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:07.269
Speaker 1: Many people going bonkers about
the reportedly accepted offer for Elon Musk

00:00:07.269 --> 00:00:09.320
to buy Twitter.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:14.299
There are people who on the right are welcoming
this with open arms, saying free speech will

00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:17.480
return to Twitter and oh, it's going to be
great.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.189
And you have people on the left saying this
is a dystopian nightmare.

00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:24.510
Let's talk through what's going on and then
I will give you my take on it.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.420
Twitter has accepted Elon Musk's buyout deal.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:33.740
The report is that Twitter's board has accepted
the offer for Elon Musk to take the company

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.740
private.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.920
Twitter's a publicly traded company right
now.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:43.210
The idea would be that Elon Musk has secured
financing at 5420 per share to buy the company

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.390
and to take it private.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.800
There were rumors floating that many said
there's no way this is happening and it appears

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.800
to be now.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.140
It still needs to actually go through the
due diligence and regulation phase and it's

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.780
possible that this will fall apart.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.180
But I'm more concerned with what the reaction
to this should be now.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:06.329
One of the problems I'm having with the reaction
for many is that it is very, very black and

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:07.329
white either.

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:11.360
This is our Elon Musk is our savior, and he's
going to save Twitter and he's going to unbanned

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.360
everybody.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.290
And Trump will be back and all of these different
things.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:17.170
And then the other side of it is that this
is the absolute worst thing that could happen

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.310
because Elon Musk is just an absolutely terrible
person.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:24.469
One of the problems that we're facing in the
United States and around the world, but in

00:01:24.469 --> 00:01:30.640
the United States, is that everything is based
around personalities and cults of personality.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.759
And I think we should resist that and we should
resist it very strongly.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:38.920
As I've said before, when it comes to elected
officials, I don't see politicians and elected

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.619
officials as being any different than you
or I. They're just people.

00:01:42.619 --> 00:01:43.640
They have some good ideas.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.649
They have some bad ideas.

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:45.649
They have good instincts.

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:46.649
They have bad instincts.

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:50.520
And we've talked about the dangerous cult
of personality around Donald Trump.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.359
But I was the first to tell you as a Bernie
supporter in 16 and 20, I didn't like the

00:01:55.359 --> 00:01:57.970
cult of personality that developed around
Bernie.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.210
Bernie can do no wrong.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.619
Oh, you don't like what he said?

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:04.000
Well, you must have misunderstood what he
said, or you're deliberately misstating what

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.000
he said.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.250
He no, he can do no wrong.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.070
Cult of personality around Tulsi Gabbard.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:12.420
There was one around Andrew Yang, there's
one around Jordan Peterson.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.720
I'm against all of it.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:18.860
We need to just see people as more nuanced
than that.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:24.700
And so when we talk about someone like Elon
Musk, that's who's at question here.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:30.670
Does Elon Musk have a history of suppressing
unionization at his companies?

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:31.670
Yeah.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.670
Yeah, and I'm against that.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:33.670
That's not good.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:40.420
Has Elon Musk dramatically accelerated the
path forward on a number of important technologies?

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:41.690
100%.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:48.040
The current rush that every manufacturer of
automobiles has not only to put out electric

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.480
vehicles, but to put out electric vehicles
whose range can match that of Tesla is only

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.950
happening because of what Elon Musk did with
Tesla and at Tesla.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.220
Bad things have also happened.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.840
There's allegations of racism, there's allegations
of union busting, all of these different things.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:09.500
But the Tesla advancement of electric vehicles
with a greater than 300 mile range as a just

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:17.690
normal thing, has led to Chevy, Ford, Audi,
Mercedes, RIVIAN, all these different companies

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:21.650
saying, hey, we got to up our game, we've
got to compete here.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.680
That's a great thing.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:30.150
When you talk about the return to space and
space X Musk reinvigorated what is now an

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:35.540
increased interest in getting back to space,
which I think is good.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:40.160
StarLink satellite internet anywhere in the
world, these are great things.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:45.710
And from a business standpoint, I've learned
it's not a good bet to bet against Elon Musk

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:47.450
when he's determined to do something.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:54.050
And he also has some terrible political instincts,
tweets, horrible things, and has all of these

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:57.900
other things that that aren't very progressive
to me.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:03.720
The track record on Free Speech, as we have
a report from CNBC about Musk's record on

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.720
free speech.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.720
It's not a great record.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:10.030
He has sought control over what journalists,
bloggers, analysts and others say about his

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:11.030
businesses.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:16.849
He's reportedly canceled people's to a bloggers
Tesla order when the blogger blogged something

00:04:16.849 --> 00:04:18.449
Elon Musk didn't like.

00:04:18.449 --> 00:04:20.310
So what does this mean for Twitter?

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.439
I have absolutely no idea.

00:04:22.439 --> 00:04:24.530
It could be bad, there's no doubt about it.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:30.389
But I think the problem I'm having is that
all of the discussion, 99% of the discussion

00:04:30.389 --> 00:04:35.199
is based around people's preexisting opinion
about Elon Musk as a uniquely great figure

00:04:35.199 --> 00:04:37.259
or is a uniquely terrible figure.

00:04:37.259 --> 00:04:38.259
And that seems.

00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:39.759
Ordinarily short sighted.

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:47.360
My main concern with Musk buying Twitter is
that of consolidation and monopoly.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:53.729
I don't really love the idea of one person
controlling so many major companies.

00:04:53.729 --> 00:04:57.069
Elon Musk's going to control Twitter.

00:04:57.069 --> 00:05:03.090
And Tesla, which is now, I believe, by market
cap, the largest auto manufacturer in the

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:10.800
United States, and SpaceX, which is, I believe,
the most important private space exploration

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.800
company.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:12.800
It started.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.979
The consolidation of power is my primary concern.

00:05:15.979 --> 00:05:20.169
Will Trump be back on Twitter as a result,
like as Elon Musk planning to unbanned Trump?

00:05:20.169 --> 00:05:21.759
I have absolutely no idea.

00:05:21.759 --> 00:05:23.680
Trump says he doesn't plan to go back on.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:24.680
That may change.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.280
That seems like a minor detail at this point.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:32.710
So let me know your thoughts about the Twitter
takeover, but try to make them substantive

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:37.379
rather than driven by just your opinion of
Elon Musk as an individual, which the right

00:05:37.379 --> 00:05:42.639
just is there praying at the altar of Musk
and it seems unhinged.

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:48.340
And also, I'm seeing some on the left who
are just painting him as a uniquely evil character,

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.219
which also doesn't strike me as accurate.

00:05:50.219 --> 00:05:51.219
Let me know your thoughts.

